A-10 package visibility, A/B on DN-ENG41 (Android 14, serial T3515NNFBC000055) and
the zxing_api36 emulator, 2026-11-02

== 1. The "share an application" picker, DN-ENG41 ==

Two APKs built from the same tree, differing only in this fix, kept side by side and
installed in turn. Scraped by tools/maint/scrape-app-picker.sh: open the SHARE screen,
tap Application, scroll in 300 px steps, collect every row label until four
consecutive dumps add nothing new.

Both counts below were produced twice, and the second time by the committed script, with
byte-identical lists. That mattered, because the measurement was wrong three times before
it was right and each failure looked like a result:

  - a fast fling skips whole screens between dumps, so the scrape silently misses rows.
    Gave 32 instead of 79, and 25 instead of 49.
  - two scrapes running at once overwrite each other's temp file and leave a plausible
    list that is neither run. Gave a 35-row file with two labels in it that are not apps.
  - `tr '>' '>\n'` does not split a line. tr pads the shorter set; it cannot expand one
    character into two. So the dump stayed one long line, `head -1` on the bounds match
    returned the root node's bounds, and the script tapped the middle of the screen and
    scraped the SHARE screen's own seven labels. It now locates the button with
    `grep -o '<node[^>]*share_app_button[^>]*>'`, and refuses to scrape at all unless
    `app_picker_list_item_label` is on screen. That guard was watched firing: on the
    broken version it printed "the app picker did not open (tapped 320,480)" and exited 1.

  before (getInstalledApplications, no <queries>): 79 rows
  after  (MAIN/LAUNCHER query + <queries>):        49 rows
  rows in both: 15

The count went down and the screen got better, which is the point.

