  So before the fix the picker listed 79 entries of which 15 were apps a user could
  launch, and 34 installed apps could not be picked at all.

  Cross-check against the platform: the device has 50 packages with a MAIN/LAUNCHER
  activity (cmd package query-activities, run from adb, which is not filtered); 49 of
  them survive the picker's own com.android.* / com.google.android.* / android /
  com.htc blocklist. The picker shows exactly those 49.

  End to end on the fixed build: tapping AsrApp -- one of the 34 that did not exist
  for this app before -- lands on the encode screen showing
  market://details?id=com.dm.ai.asrapp.

== 2. resolveActivity in launchProductQuery, zxing_api36 emulator ==

DN-ENG41 has no browser at all: nothing on it answers VIEW https, so the special case
in launchProductQuery cannot be exercised there either way. The API 36 emulator has
com.android.chrome, which is one of the two packages that code names.

dumpsys package queries, the block listing what this app can see through its intent
queries, same two APKs:

  without <queries>: 0 packages
  with <queries>:    21 packages, com.android.chrome among them:
    com.android.camera2
    com.android.chrome
    com.google.android.apps.accessibility.voiceaccess
    com.google.android.apps.docs
    com.google.android.apps.maps
    com.google.android.apps.messaging
    com.google.android.apps.photos
    com.google.android.apps.safetyhub
    com.google.android.apps.youtube.music
    com.google.android.calendar
    com.google.android.cellbroadcastreceiver
    com.google.android.contacts
    com.google.android.deskclock
    com.google.android.dialer
    com.google.android.documentsui
    com.google.android.gm
    com.google.android.googlequicksearchbox
    com.google.android.inputmethod.latin
    com.google.android.projection.gearhead
    com.google.android.youtube
    queryable via interaction:

That set is what resolveActivity reads, so the special case can match again.

NOT verified: the product-search flow running end to end. It needs a product barcode
scanned after a PRODUCT_SEARCH_LINK or zxing:// launch, and the virtual-scene camera
could not be aimed at the poster from the command line -- adb emu offers
virtualscene-image but no macro command, and the scene's default view does not face
the wall.
